Dr. Khalifa: So, this is to everybody, including the messengers. Yeah.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:41.000
Catherine: Verse 64

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:59.000
[3:64] Say, "O followers of the scripture, let us come to a logical agreement between us and you: that we do not worship except GOD; that we never set up any idols beside Him, and never set up each other as gods beside GOD." If they reject such an agreement, then say, "Bear witness that we are Muslims."

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:07.000
[3:65] O followers of the scripture, why do you argue about Abraham, when the Torah and the Gospel were not revealed until after him? Do you not understand?

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:15.000
[3:66] You have argued about things you knew, but why do you argue about things you don't know? GOD knows, while you do not know.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.000
I'm gonna stop here and go back to 64.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:27.000
A major error that we make, and, and I have to include me in that, is that in casual speech, we attribute

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:33.000
anything and all kinds of things to other people. Even to the driver, as we're driving along, who cuts in front of us too

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:40.000
close. And we say "why did he do that?" Nothing happens that isn't God's doing.

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:46.000
To attribute anything, Rashad uses the, frequently, the example of anything to our boss.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:54.000
If we get a raise, it came from the boss. If we got chastised, it came from that person. And it has not come from

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:59.000
that person. It has come from God. It's designed for us. And, and it's millions of little ways that

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:04.000
we can remember God every day. My son has just gotten a car recently and has learned to drive,

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:09.000
for example. And there are times when people do some really foolish things on the road. And

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:15.000
he gets very angry, very quickly. And then after that second, he'll turn around and say,

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:21.000
"God did this and I don't need to be angry about it. I need to be a better driver." Alhamdu Lillah,

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:27.000
that will happen. But that's just a minor example that every day in our lives someone will come into

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:32.000
my office, for example, and bring me a book to read. And it will turn out to be something

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:38.000
that I need or have questions about. For example, Edip recently gave a Khutba and was talking about the

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:46.000
decimal places in Pi. And I remember studying that in high school. It so happens that at that

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:51.000
point I got the Reader's Digest at home and there was an incredible article about an Indian man

00:13:51.000 --> 00:14:00.000
who memorized 38,000 of those decimal places so far. And he had a favorite section from the 2,000th to

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:07.000
the 3,000th. He liked that section particularly well. So, those kinds of things don't happen

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:13.000
by accident. Everything that happens to us, we need to remember, does not happen as a result of

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:18.000
another person, but as a result of God designing our lives for us to bring us to the truth.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:24.000
I can't imagine why anyone would want to know that many decimal places in Pi.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:36.000
And in verse 66, 65 and 66, the reason for argument is many, but it always boils down to ego.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:43.000
People's ego is affected if they need to argue, especially about things they don't know.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:50.000
They don't want to appear foolish or they want to obtain something that they don't think is already there, either control of other people

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:57.000
or some status or some power, or to appear different in people's eyes than they really are. So, ego is

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:03.000
almost always involved. And the question about why do we argue about things we don't know is because

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:08.000
we're bad. We're gonna argue about things we don't know. We're going to find a way to justify

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:16.000
what we're doing, even if it's, even if it's saying something we don't know or implying that we know something we don't know.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:20.000
It's one of the reasons that we need to be extraordinarily careful when we are talking

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:26.000
to that people, to people about the Quran and about God alone. We do really need to know what we're talking about.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:30.000
And when questions are asked of us that we don't have at our fingertips, we need to research them

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:36.000
and go back with the correct answer and not guess. And again, I speak from personal experience. I

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:41.000
recently have found myself having to say "I don't know. Let me look it up because I don't know." Or

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:48.000
"let me ask." And to get into arguments with people who are, and I've had this experience, too.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:52.000
Someone who's extraordinarily well-versed in the Bible, the New Testament or the Old Testament,

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:58.000
I'm not. And I don't have the Quran committed to memory. I need to look things up in the Quran,

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:04.000
frequently. So, for me to argue with those people is fruitless. I mean, there's just nowhere for me to go.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:11.000
So, the point is made that we need to know exactly what we're discussing and not to pretend

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:19.000
Catherine: to know something we don't know. Does anyone have something to add? Or enlarge the Quran in those few verses?

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:27.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, I don't think we can pass up 64 without emphasizing this suggestion, this Suggestion from God. It says,

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:30.000
[3:64] Say, "O followers of the scriptures, ...

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.000
Jews and Christins

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.000
[3:64] ... let us come to a logical agreement ...

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:34.000
that we worship God alone.

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:40.000
So, why shouldn't any Christian or Jew accept this?

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:46.000
What is wrong with this idea of worshiping the One who created us, the One who created the heavens and

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:51.000
the earth, the One who controls our happiness and joy and provisions?

00:16:53.000 --> 00:17:01.000
Why, why, why do you think a Christian will not accept this suggestion? "Let us worship God alone and forget the human factors,

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:08.000
Muhammad and Jesus and Mary and so on. The only reason a Christian will reject or a Jew will reject

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:12.000
a suggestion like this would be ego. "How will I face my friends?"

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:19.000
"I'm gonna tell my friends, my relatives, my parents that I don't care about the humans anymore, I only worship God."

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:28.000
"I don't care if Jesus is this or that or if Muhammad is this or that." Therefore, that person is worshiping

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:32.000
his or her ego. It's a logical agreement.

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:35.000
"O, Christians and Jews"

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:43.000
[3:64] ... let us come to a logical agreement between us and you: that we do not worship except GOD; that we never set up any idols besides Him, ...

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:50.000
We come to the realization that idols have no power to benefit you or harm you.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:56.000
The idols have nothing to do with controlling the rotation of the sun or the moon or the earth,

00:17:56.000 --> 00:18:03.000
or the length of day and night, or providing for you. In Sura 29, we read

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:12.000
that the idols you idolize possess no provisions for you. So, seek the provisions from God alone. They can do nothing for us.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:20.000
So, the agreement is do not worship except God and we never set up any idols beside Him,

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:27.000
and never set up each other as gods beside God. When God tells me that the ablution is 4 steps,

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:35.000
and some other Mulla tells me the ablution is 9 steps, if I do the 9 steps, I'm setting up this Mulla or teacher as a god.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:44.000
The teachings that you follow come from your god. If you follow the teachings

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:50.000
given to us by God, you're worshiping God. So, this very logical agreement.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:19:02.000
And the only reason any Jew or Christian or Hindu or Buddhist would reject it would be ego. And we learn from Quran that

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:08.000
the majority of people in Hell are there because they went along with their relatives or friends.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:13.000
The Arabic is (29:25) مَّوَدَّةَ بَيْنِكُمْ فِى ٱلْحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنْيَا

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:20.000
Because of your friendship in this life, you sacrifice your Eternal happiness which begins here.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:26.000
So, you can see the, the logic of it.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:34.000
We have to be guarding, we have to be very sensitive to the fact that God adorns

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:41.000
the people's beliefs in their eyes. And so, we have to examine our own beliefs. Are we... How do we know we

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:47.000
are not way off and God is adorning our way in our eyes? How do we know? We have to examine ourselves critically.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:54.000
And you have to examine the logic of your belief, critically. You have to be critical of yourself.

00:19:55.000 --> 00:20:00.000
Until you prove that you are not an idol worshipper. You have to start with the assumption

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:05.000
that you are an idol-worshipper, that you're not on the right path. And try very hard to prove

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:08.000
this. If you fail, then you're okay.

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.000
So, it's all logic.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:21.000
